SLUG: services/home-shifting.html
TITLE: Home Shifting in Kanpur — full household moves
DESC: Full household shifting in Kanpur: room-by-room inventory, professional packing, furniture dismantled and reassembled, loaded, moved and placed in the new home.
HEADING: Home shifting
LEAD: A full household move, run room by room against a written inventory — packed, dismantled, loaded, moved, rebuilt and placed where you want it.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Services|/services.html ; Home shifting|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <h2>What a home shift actually involves</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            The work starts well before the truck. A household move is mostly
            a counting and sequencing problem: knowing exactly what is going,
            packing it so it survives the journey, and loading it in an order
            that lets it come off in the right rooms.
          </p>
          <p>
            We survey first — in person or over a video call — and produce a
            room-by-room inventory. That inventory decides the vehicle size,
            the crew size, how much packing material is loaded the night
            before, and the quote. It is also what gets signed at both ends,
            so anything missing is obvious on the day rather than a week later.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-home"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Included as standard</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Room-by-room inventory, written and shared with you</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Multi-layer packing for glass, crockery and electronics</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Beds, wardrobes and modular units dismantled and reassembled</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Hardware bagged and taped to the item it came off</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Cartons labelled by room and contents</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Placement in the right room at the new home, not dumped in the hall</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">How it runs</span>
        <h2>The day, in order</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps grid grid-2">
        <li class="step"><div>
          <h3>Crew briefing and protection</h3>
          <p>The team arrives with your inventory already in hand. Floors and door frames on the route out are protected before anything moves.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="step"><div>
          <h3>Packing, kitchen first</h3>
          <p>The kitchen takes the longest and is packed first. Fragile items are wrapped individually, then boxed with fill so nothing shifts inside the carton.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="step"><div>
          <h3>Dismantling</h3>
          <p>Beds, wardrobes and tables come apart. Screws and fittings go into a labelled bag taped to the frame they belong to.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="step"><div>
          <h3>Loading</h3>
          <p>Heavy and flat items go in first and low. Fragile cartons ride on top. The load is strapped in sections so nothing shifts in transit.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="step"><div>
          <h3>Transport</h3>
          <p>A vehicle sized to your inventory. You get the driver's number, and your coordinator stays reachable for the whole journey.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="step"><div>
          <h3>Unload, rebuild, check</h3>
          <p>Unloaded by room against the same inventory, furniture reassembled, and the list signed off with you before the crew leaves.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>What changes the price</h2>
          <p class="lead">Four things, in roughly this order of impact.</p>
          <ol class="steps mt-6">
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>How much there is</h3>
              <p>Volume decides the vehicle and the crew. A 3 BHK that has been lived in for ten years is a different job from one occupied for two.</p>
            </div></li>
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>How much packing you want</h3>
              <p>Full packing is the single largest line on most quotes. Packing your own clothes, books and linen typically takes a meaningful amount off it.</p>
            </div></li>
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>Access at both ends</h3>
              <p>A fourth floor without a lift needs more people, not more hours. So does a long carry from the gate to the door.</p>
            </div></li>
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>The date</h3>
              <p>Month-end is when everyone moves. Mid-month dates are easier to staff and usually cheaper.</p>
            </div></li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>Questions we get asked</h2>
          <div class="faq mt-6" data-faq>
            <details>
              <summary>How long does a 2 BHK take?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                With full packing, usually a day to pack and load and a second
                for delivery and reassembly on a local route — or the same day
                end to end if you have packed most of it yourself. The survey
                gives you a real answer for your flat rather than an average.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Can you move just a few rooms?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                Yes. Part-household moves are common — one bedroom's worth of
                furniture going to a different city, for example. It is priced
                on the inventory, not on the size of the flat it came from.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Will you take the packing material away?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                Yes, if you want it gone. We can unpack and remove the empty
                cartons and wrap on the same visit, or come back for them once
                you have unpacked at your own pace.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>What about the fridge and washing machine?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                Defrost and drain the fridge the night before, and drain the
                washing machine's hoses. We move them wrapped and upright.
                Appliances that need a technician to disconnect or install —
                a split AC, for example — are a separate job we can arrange.
              </p></div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


